[h1]Cosmic Chronicles[/h1]
[i]A Dynamic Narrative & Living Galaxy Expansion Mod[/i]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]📰 v3.2.0: The News Board, Rebuilt[/h2]
The Galactic News Network just got a full newsroom upgrade: category filters, live search, a sortable 3-column headline table, unread tracking, and a Breaking News banner with an instant chat alert. That banner is reserved for events that actually matter: Behemoth incursions, boss kills, and a brand-new tracker that reports the exact moment an AI empire is wiped out. Cosmic War bounty completions and faction ceasefires now show up on the board too, and every headline shows how long ago it broke.

[hr][/hr]

[h2]What does this mod do?[/h2]
Avorion's background simulations run deep, but they rarely get a voice. [b]Cosmic Chronicles[/b] turns the math behind wars and economies into stories, without bloating server memory. Jump into a high-War-Heat sector and the locals sound scared. Walk into a booming economy and the merchants brag about it.

[b]⚠️ REQUIRED DEPENDENCIES:[/b]
This mod needs live data from the following mods to function:
1. [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3727542782]Cosmic Vault[/url]
2. [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3315794988]Cosmic Overhaul[/url]
3. [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3727544356]Cosmic War[/url]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]Highlighted Features[/h2]
👉 [b][url=https://github.com/Stormiebox/Cosmic-Chronicles/wiki/Players-Guide-The-Living-Galaxy]Read the Player's Guide on the Wiki[/url][/b]

[list]
[*]🗣️ [b]The Rumormonger:[/b] 60+ lines of interactive rumors, ambient chatter, and station-specific dialogue, plus in-character tutorial tips.
[*]📰 [b]Galactic News Network:[/b] a searchable, filterable newsroom with category grouping, unread tracking, relative headline ages, and Breaking News alerts.
[*]🧑‍✈️ [b]Captain Synergies:[/b] your captain's class changes how events play out. Scavengers pull more loot, Merchants negotiate hazard pay, Smugglers talk their way past hostile ports.
[*]🚀 [b]Refugee Convoys:[/b] fleeing civilians appear in high-War-Heat sectors. Donate resources to rescue them and earn reputation.
[*]🏚️ [b]Echoes of the Frontline:[/b] find massive, persistent derelict graveyards in sectors that just fought a war.
[*]📦 [b]Black Box Extraction:[/b] pull audio logs, system upgrades, and scaling credit rewards out of derelict graveyards. Watch for classified Rift Tech contraband among the loot.
[*]🏛️ [b]Cinematic Monuments:[/b] discover procedural monuments deep in AI territory. Reading the inscription grants a permanent +2,500 reputation boost.
[*]👻 [b]Drifting Ghost Ships & Ancient Data Caches:[/b] intercept a derelict freighter's dying transmission, or trade encrypted log fragments from an ancient vault at any Research Station.
[*]🤖 [b]Rogue AI Probes & Stranded Diplomats:[/b] chase down a probe before it hyperspaces away with your sector data, or extract a diplomat before their captors do.
[*]📜 [b]Captain's Logs:[/b] send a captain on a Cosmic Overhaul background mission and their mail report comes back with a narrative log describing what actually happened out there.
[*]🛑 [b]Smart Anti-Spam:[/b] ambient chatter runs on a global cooldown, so chat never floods.
[/list]

✅ [b]Fully localized:[/b] Chinese, German, Russian, Portuguese, French, Japanese, and Spanish, via Avorion's deferred translation engine.

[hr][/hr]

[h2]🌌 Cosmic Vault Synergy[/h2]
Everything above runs on the same shared APIs as the rest of the series. Ambient News events raise or lower a faction's Famine Score through the Vault economy, destroyed empires get filtered out of News generation instead of broadcasting from beyond the grave, and defeating the Bottan Dreadnought spawns a persistent Spatial Rift anomaly for advanced exploration. All of it is also readable in-game from the Cosmic Codex, so you never have to alt-tab to check a wiki mid-session.

[hr][/hr]

[h2]❓ FAQs & Compatibility[/h2]
[quote]
[b]Can I install this mid-playthrough?[/b]
[b]YES.[/b] [i]Cosmic War[/i] scans your save and generates the faction data the Rumormonger needs, so it has plenty to talk about right away.

[b]Can I remove this mod mid-game?[/b]
[b]NO.[/b] It alters save games by attaching scripts (Rumormonger, Captain's Logs) to entities. Removing it mid-game floods your error log and can corrupt save state.
[/quote]

[b]⚠️ INCOMPATIBILITIES:[/b]
[url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2923179923]Xavorion: eXtended Avorion[/url] - overrides the game's core fundamentals and is fully incompatible.

